==English==

===Etymology===
Probably alteration of {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|taïaut||pos=interjection used in deer-hunting|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|tahou|lang=frm}}, {{term|tayo|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|taho|lang=fro}}, {{term|ta ho|lang=fro}}, {{term|tielau||pos=interjection given to hounds to return|lang=fro}}, composed of {{term||ta|pos=particle used to prod animals|lang=fro}} + {{term|ho|ho !|halt!, hold!|lang=fro}}. More at {{l|en|ho}}.

===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# {{UK}} used to [[urge]] on a [[fox hunt]], especially when the [[fox]] is [[sight]]ed.
#: ''There he is! Coming out of that coppice! '''Tallyho tallyho tallyho'''!''
# a simple greeting, exclusively used by the [[upper class]]es.
#: '''''Tallyho''' chaps! What's the time, anybody?''

====See also====
* {{pedialite|Tally-ho}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# the interjection.
#: ''Alright, I'll give them the old '''tallyho'''.''

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# to articulate the interjection.
#: ''I'll '''tallyho''' once we've got to the top.''

